0 Screenshot sample: small house
0 Name: screenshot-sample.ldr
0 Author: LeoCAD Harmony port (member C, D11)
0
0 VERTICAL CONVENTION -- this is what was wrong in the first revision.
0 ---------------------------------------------------------------------
0 An LDraw part's origin sits on its TOP face: a 2x4 brick occupies
0 y = 0..24 BELOW its origin, with studs sticking up to y = -4. LDraw Y grows
0 DOWNWARD, and LeoCAD preserves that when converting
0 (common/lc_math.h lcVector3LDrawToLeoCAD maps (x, y, z) to (x, z, -y)),
0 so a LARGER y is LOWER on screen. Stacking upward therefore means counting
0 DOWN: each course above another has a smaller y than the one below.
0 The first revision counted up, which placed the roof under the walls and the
0 chimney under that. Existence checks on part ids and colours cannot see that;
0 the geometry check in verify_sample_model.py can.
0
0 Measured from assets/ldraw-lite/library-lite.zip:
0   3001 brick 2x4, 3003 brick 2x2, 3004 brick 1x2: body 0..24, studs -4..0
0   3035 plate 4x8:                                body 0..8,  studs -4..0
0
0 Resulting stack (top face of each layer):
0   base plate  top    0  body    0..8
0   wall 1      top  -24  body  -24..0     rests on the base plate
0   wall 2      top  -48  body  -48..-24   rests on wall 1
0   roof        top  -56  body  -56..-48   rests on wall 2
0   chimney     top  -80  body  -80..-56   rests on the roof
0   chimney 2   top -104  body -104..-80   rests on the chimney
0
0 Footprint: 8x8 studs, x -80..80, z -80..80. Walls are one stud thick (20).
0 Front and back walls span x -60..60 so the corners belong to the side walls;
0 that keeps four groups from interpenetrating at the corners.
0 ---------------------------------------------------------------------
0
